Z||000000||gabriel||03-05-2001||10:40 AM||||  I'm still casting about for header info on headers for the 3800SC.<P>   The ones at Thrasher have some good dyno slips to backup the claims of increased HP/torque, however, of course, they won't fit a Fiero swap.<P>   Has anyone used the headers for the 3800SC from Chris West?<P>   His headers look nice, but has anyone dynoed this item?  My initial concern is that item doesn't seem to be useing equal length tubing from the ports to the collectors.<BR>It's hard to tell from the pictures, but Thrasher seems to be pretty close ...<P>   Otherwise I'll still try to fabricate a set, but it would need lots of testing work on a dyno.<P>  Oh, BTW, Terryk mentioned to check "The Buick Power Book."  I can't find it anywhere.  Is that the correct title?<P>    -Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Will||03-05-2001||10:53 AM||||Have you read "The Scientific Design of Exhasut and Intake Systems" by Morrison and Smith? I'm not thoroughly read on the subject yet, but that book was quite helpful. Amazon has it here:<BR><A HREF="http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0837603099/qid%3D983807399/103-5750957-0945459" TARGET=_blank> <A HREF="http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0837603099/qid%3D983807399/103-5750957-0945459" TARGET=_blank>http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0837603099/qid%3D983807399/103-5750957-0945459</A>  </A><BR>||||reg||1
