Z||000005||gabriel||03-07-2001||03:33 PM||||Hello.<BR>&gt;well, we have them in stock if you wish to proceed with your project<P>&gt;like any other bolt on, it all depends on the motor <P>  Thanks, Chris, I'm seriously considering your product.  Absolutely, I would rebuild the engine before final install & mods. <P>&gt;The book is the Buick Power Source. A GM Publication. Page 138-141.<P>Thanks Terryk, I'll ask for it & see what they say. I'll try Thrasher, as well, but I'm not holding my breath!<P>  I was actually thinking about true dual exhaust, & I wonder if that might work out better than a y-pipe.  I can foresee an issue or two there.   I had once read an article on a Magneson (sp?) upgrade to this blower that was supposed to show a torque increase across the RPM range.<P>Has anyone had experience w/this item?<P>Also, has anyone used that Dyno program by Mr. Gasket?  I have read a few  good reviews regarding it.  -Thanks.<P> <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||GTallen||03-12-2001||12:05 AM||||The Magnusen drive completely replaces the SC nose drive with a keyed shaft type nose.  So that your pulley can be removed and changed in a couple of minutes.  It isn't that expensive, comparably.  Dial-Ur-Boost also makes a nice setup.  They used a common pulley base that has interchangeable diameters.  Remove four allen-head bolts, swap, retighten and your off.||||reg||1
Z||000007||terryk||03-12-2001||07:27 PM||||I know that Mangnusen will s-port M-90 blowers and improve the flow. They are expensive but very good.||||reg||1
